ti-adas-firmware (1.0.0-4) noble; urgency=medium

  * debian/ti-adas-firmware.links: re-add firmware symlinks as tracked
    package files (via dh_link) rather than postinst update-alternatives.
    Creates /usr/lib/firmware/j784s4-{main-r5f0_0..r5f2_1,c71_0..c71_3}-fw
    pointing to vision_apps_evm/vx_app_rtos_linux_*.out.
    Safe with dorprocboot=0: U-Boot does not auto-load firmware at boot so
    the RTOS RTI watchdog timers are never armed without the vision_apps
    IPC stack present.
  * debian/control: fix description — only unsigned .out files are shipped;
    remove incorrect mention of signed variants.

 -- Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>  Sat, 17 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000

ti-adas-firmware (1.0.0-3) noble; urgency=medium

  * postinst/prerm: remove all update-alternatives calls.
    Creating /usr/lib/firmware/j784s4-*-fw symlinks at install time causes
    the kernel remoteproc subsystem to auto-boot all 10 DSP/MCU cores
    (auto_boot=true is the kernel default). The RTOS firmware activates RTI
    hardware watchdog timers; without the vision_apps stack feeding them the
    watchdog fires a hardware SoC reset, causing a boot loop.
    Firmware files remain in /usr/lib/firmware/vision_apps_evm/ and are
    available for userspace remoteproc management when vision_apps is used.

 -- Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>  Fri, 16 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000

ti-adas-firmware (1.0.0-2) noble; urgency=medium

  * postinst/prerm: remove .out.signed update-alternatives entries;
    signed firmware blobs are not included in the package, causing
    update-alternatives to fail with "path doesn't exist" error.

 -- Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>  Fri, 09 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000

ti-adas-firmware (1.0.0-1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging of TI vision_apps RTOS firmware for j784s4-evm.
    Built from psdk_fw.git SRCREV 579af7d6 (PSDK Analytics 11.02).
    Includes R5F MCU (mcu2_0/1, mcu3_0/1, mcu4_0/1) and C7x DSP
    (c7x_1/2/3/4) firmware, both unsigned and signed variants.

 -- Vijay Pothukuchi <vijayp@ti.com>  Thu, 08 May 2025 00:00:00 +0000
